<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
T0.2 reference scenario — connections.

Explicit lane-to-lane connections, written by hand rather than left to netconvert's default
guesser, because the point of this ticket is to understand the format.

Lane layout per approach (2 lanes, 0 = rightmost per 05_DOMAIN_MODEL.md §7):
  lane 0 (right/outer): through + right turn
  lane 1 (left/inner):  through only

No left-turn connections exist in this network. D-023 point 4 restricts M1 scenarios to
protected turns only, and the only way to run a *left* turn as protected with just the two
phases (NS, EW) this ticket specifies would be to give the opposing through movement a
separate phase (4 phases) or a leading/lagging arrow — out of scope here. Through and right
turns are the only movements that are simultaneously (a) always geometrically non-conflicting
with each other on a 2-phase NS/EW split and (b) protected. Omitting left turns is therefore
not a simplification of convenience; it is the only way to satisfy "two phases" and
"protected turns only" at once. See research/M0_reference_scenario.md Q4 for a second,
throwaway network (spikes/M0_reference/conflict_probe/) that adds a left-turn lane purely to
inspect how SUMO represents the resulting permitted/conflicting relationship.

Right-hand traffic. Directions below are the compass direction of travel through C.
-->
<connections>
    <!-- North approach (N2C), travelling south -->
    <connection from="N2C" to="C2S" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>   <!-- through -->
    <connection from="N2C" to="C2S" fromLane="1" toLane="1"/>   <!-- through -->
    <connection from="N2C" to="C2W" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>   <!-- right turn -->

    <!-- South approach (S2C), travelling north -->
    <connection from="S2C" to="C2N" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>   <!-- through -->
    <connection from="S2C" to="C2N" fromLane="1" toLane="1"/>   <!-- through -->
    <connection from="S2C" to="C2E" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>   <!-- right turn -->

    <!-- East approach (E2C), travelling west -->
    <connection from="E2C" to="C2W" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>   <!-- through -->
    <connection from="E2C" to="C2W" fromLane="1" toLane="1"/>   <!-- through -->
    <connection from="E2C" to="C2N" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>   <!-- right turn -->

    <!-- West approach (W2C), travelling east -->
    <connection from="W2C" to="C2E" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>   <!-- through -->
    <connection from="W2C" to="C2E" fromLane="1" toLane="1"/>   <!-- through -->
    <connection from="W2C" to="C2S" fromLane="0" toLane="0"/>   <!-- right turn -->
</connections>
